  "id": "Compound::DB01424 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Aminophenazone appears to interact with multiple cytochrome P450 enzymes, specifically Cyp2c9 and Cyp1a2, through binding interactions. These enzymes are involved in the metabolism of various substrates, including arachidonic acid, which is a key precursor in the biosynthesis of pro-inflammatory mediators. The observed pathway links Aminophenazone to Cyp2d6 via a series of enzymatic activities, suggesting that Aminophenazone may influence the metabolic capacity of Cyp2d6 through indirect mechanisms. The shared involvement of Cyp2d6 in the metabolism of arachidonic acid, as indicated by the participation of Cyp2c9 and Cyp1a2, implies that Aminophenazone may modulate Cyp2d6 activity by affecting the metabolic pathways it is involved in. This integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Aminophenazone and Cyp2d6, where the drug may exert its effects through the modulation of enzymatic activities that ultimately influence the metabolic processing of arachidonic acid. The presence of multiple pathways and the consistent scores across different paths suggest a robust and biologically plausible mechanism of action.",
